// windowing_demo_v2: DESIGN DRAFT for std::windowing, a GLFW-style window and input module in the
// standard library, with several windows per program. Nothing here compiles yet: this file shows
// what using the API would look like, so the API can be reviewed before any of it is built.
// Supersedes drafts/windowing_demo.rifts (one window, written before specs 26-31).
//
// The program opens:
//   - a game window (OpenGL 3.3, redrawn every frame),
//   - inspector windows on Ctrl+N (tool windows owned by the game window, redrawn only on demand),
//     which join the game window's share group, so a texture uploaded once is usable in all of them,
//   - a sandbox window on Ctrl+Shift+N (OpenGL 2.1, independent: shares nothing).
// A background thread builds an image; the main thread uploads it once into the shared group.
// A stand-in for the future debug UI shows where that UI plugs in (input routing + drawing).
//
// ================================================================================================
// Design decisions, and the spec rule each one comes from
// ================================================================================================
//  1. RAII, not init/terminate. wnd::system::start() replaces glfwInit. Every window holds a
//     counted reference to the platform connection, so the connection closes when `sys` *and*
//     every window are gone (12). Destruction order no longer matters, and a window moved into a
//     longer-lived place can't outlive the connection (old draft, open question 3).
//  2. One queue per window. sys.poll() reads the OS queue once and sorts each event into the
//     queue of the window it belongs to. win.drain_events(mut buffer) moves them into a darray the
//     caller owns, so nothing borrows `sys` or `win` while the events are handled (12): handlers
//     can call `mut` methods on the window. The buffer keeps its capacity: no allocation per frame
//     once it has grown (principle 7). Events that belong to no window (monitors, gamepads) go to
//     sys.drain_events(...). Events are copy-type enum values matched exhaustively (08, 10); there
//     are no callbacks (no std::function on the heap, no reference captures that would make the
//     window a view, 18).
//  3. Windows are independent by default in everything that isn't a GPU resource: own queue, own
//     input state, own cursor mode, own swap interval, own redraw policy, own close flag.
//  4. GPU resources are shared whenever they can be. `window_config.sharing` (05, a field with a
//     default) says how:
//        sharing::automatic    (default) join an existing share group whose OpenGL config is
//                              compatible, otherwise start a new one
//        sharing::join(group)  must join this group; error share_incompatible otherwise
//        sharing::independent  a group of its own, never shared
//     A share group is a counted handle (`.clone()` makes the cost visible, 13). It owns a hidden
//     1x1 context, so resources can be uploaded before any window exists and survive when windows
//     close. Monitors, cursors and the clipboard belong to the system and are shared by all
//     windows anyway. A Vulkan program (graphics::none) shares its VkDevice across windows
//     itself; std::windowing only makes one surface per window.
//  5. A current GL context is a value. win.begin_gl_frame() makes the window's context current and
//     returns a wnd::gl_frame, a view that borrows the window exclusively (12): the window can't
//     be resized, closed or moved away mid-frame. frame.present() swaps and is a consuming method
//     (`move`, 27 §9). share_group.make_current() returns a wnd::gl_current for work without a
//     window. Only one context per thread may be current: making a second one current while a
//     frame or gl_current is alive panics in debug-based modes with both locations, like the
//     mutex re-lock check (27 §5, run_time(std::build::mode::debug) check).
//  6. Main thread only. wnd::system, wnd::window, wnd::share_group, wnd::gl_frame hold a
//     std::thread_bound field, so moving one to another thread is a compile error (27 §1, example
//     5). Plain data (wnd::image, wnd::event, wnd::key, ...) is sendable: images can be made on
//     worker threads and handed over through a channel (this demo does).
//  7. Config is a struct, not glfwWindowHint state: designated fields with defaults (05). Errors
//     are values: creation returns std::result<T, wnd::error> (11). Changes are visible: anything
//     that changes a window is a `mut` method (06).
//  8. Time comes from std::time (instant, duration), not from the windowing module: one way (20).
//  9. Short names without `using`: a file-local namespace alias, `namespace wnd = std::windowing;`
//     (30). This closes open question 1 of the old draft.
//
// ================================================================================================
// Hooks for the debug UI (immediate and retained mode). Not designed here, only kept possible.
// ================================================================================================
//  a. Input routing. interface wnd::input_layer { routing on_event(event e, window& win) mut; }
//     wnd::route(mut events, mut layer, win) offers every event to the layer first and removes
//     the ones it answers with routing::consume. The game then sees only what the UI left.
//  b. Input snapshot for immediate mode. win.input() is a wnd::input_state&: keys and buttons held,
//     pressed/released since the last drain_events, cursor position, scroll and text of this
//     frame, modifiers. It is the raw device state; a UI that wants the keyboard says so through
//     its own wants_keyboard(), like ImGui's WantCaptureKeyboard.
//  c. Drawing in the same frame. A gl_frame can be drawn into by several renderers before
//     present(): the app first, the UI last. frame.window() gives the size and content scale.
//  d. Retained mode / tool windows. window_config.redraw = redraw::on_demand: such a window is only
//     drawn after win.request_redraw(), an expose, a resize or a scale change (win.should_draw()).
//     sys.wait() / wait_for(d) sleep until something happens, so idle tools cost nothing.
//  e. Multiple viewports. A panel dragged out of the game window becomes a window of kind
//     window_kind::popup(owner) (no decoration, no taskbar entry, no focus on show). It joins the
//     owner's share group automatically, so the UI's font atlas is uploaded once for all viewports.
//  f. What a UI needs from the platform: cursor shapes (wnd::cursor_shape::ibeam over text),
//     clipboard text, text input with win.set_text_input_area(rect) for IME placement,
//     content scale per window and per monitor.
//  g. Bindings by reflection. This demo binds keys with an @binding annotation on methods (29); a
//     debug UI can list every binding of a type with std::meta::methods<T>() (26), so a "keys"
//     panel never goes out of date.
//
// ================================================================================================
// API sketch (only what this demo uses; the .rifth comes after the review)
// ================================================================================================
//  namespace std::windowing {
//      class system {                                  // glfwInit / glfwTerminate
//          static std::result<system, error> start();  // error::already_started on a second call
//          platform platform();                        // wayland, x11, win32, cocoa
//          std::span<monitor> monitors();
//          std::option<monitor_id> primary_monitor();
//          std::result<window, error>       create_window(window_config config) mut;
//          std::result<share_group, error>  create_share_group(opengl_config config) mut;
//          void poll() mut;                            // glfwPollEvents
//          void wait() mut;                            // glfwWaitEvents
//          void wait_for(std::time::duration limit) mut;    // glfwWaitEventsTimeout
//          void drain_events(mut std::darray<system_event>& out) mut;
//          std::option<gamepad_state> gamepad(u8 slot);
//          std::option<std::string> clipboard_text();
//          void set_clipboard_text(std::str text) mut;
//      }
//      class window {
//          window_id id();
//          void drain_events(mut std::darray<event>& out) mut;   // also starts a new input frame
//          input_state& input();
//          bool should_close();  void request_close() mut;  void cancel_close() mut;
//          bool should_draw();   void request_redraw() mut;
//          gl_frame begin_gl_frame() mut;              // makes the context current
//          std::option<share_group_id> share_group_id();
//          void set_title(std::str title) mut;   void set_icon(image& icon) mut;
//          void set_cursor_mode(cursor_mode mode) mut;  void set_cursor(cursor_style style) mut;
//          window_mode mode();  void enter_fullscreen(monitor_id m) mut;  void leave_fullscreen() mut;
//          size size();  size framebuffer_size();  scale content_scale();  rect rect();
//          std::darray<std::filesystem::path> take_dropped_files() mut;   // allocates, on request
//      }
//      class share_group : std::cloneable { share_group_id id(); gl_current make_current();
//                                           std::option<std::raw_ptr<u8>> proc_address(std::str name); }
//      view class gl_frame   { window& window(); size framebuffer_size(); void present() move; }
//      view class gl_current { }                       // proof that a context is current
//      view struct window_config { std::str title; size size; std::option<point> position;
//          bool resizable, decorated, visible, focus_on_show, transparent, always_on_top;
//          window_kind kind; graphics graphics; sharing sharing; redraw redraw; }
//      enum graphics : u8 { none, opengl(opengl_config) }
//      enum sharing : u8 { automatic, join(share_group), independent }
//      enum window_kind : u8 { normal, tool(window_id), popup(window_id) }
//      enum redraw : u8 { continuous, on_demand }
//      enum event : u8 { close_requested, key(key_event), text(char), mouse_button(mouse_button_event),
//          cursor_moved(position), cursor_entered(bool), scrolled(position), resized(size),
//          framebuffer_resized(size), content_scale_changed(scale), moved(point),
//          focus_changed(bool), minimized(bool), maximized(bool), files_dropped, redraw_requested }
//      enum system_event : u8 { monitor_connected(monitor_id), monitor_disconnected(monitor_id),
//          gamepad_connected(u8), gamepad_disconnected(u8) }
//      interface input_layer { routing on_event(event e, window& win) mut; }
//      template<type L : input_layer> void route(mut std::darray<event>& events, mut L& layer, window& win);
//  }
//
// ================================================================================================
// GLFW → std::windowing
// ================================================================================================
//  glfwInit / glfwTerminate            wnd::system::start() / last owner destroyed
//  glfwWindowHint + glfwCreateWindow   sys.create_window(wnd::window_config{ ... })
//  glfwCreateWindow(..., share)        .sharing = wnd::sharing::automatic / join(group) / independent
//  glfwDestroyWindow                   ~window() (drop it, e.g. darray.retain)
//  glfwPollEvents / glfwWaitEvents     sys.poll() / sys.wait() / sys.wait_for(d), then win.drain_events
//  glfwSet*Callback                    wnd::event alternatives; wnd::input_layer for layered input
//  glfwGetKey / glfwGetMouseButton     win.input().key_down(k) / .mouse_down(b) (+ pressed/released)
//  glfwMakeContextCurrent              win.begin_gl_frame() / group.make_current() (values, not state)
//  glfwSwapBuffers                     frame.present()
//  glfwSwapInterval                    win.set_swap_interval(n) mut (per window: it is per context)
//  glfwSetWindowMonitor                win.enter_fullscreen(monitor) / win.leave_fullscreen()
//  glfwSetDropCallback                 event::files_dropped + win.take_dropped_files()
//  glfwSetMonitorCallback              wnd::system_event via sys.drain_events
//  glfwGetTime                         std::time::instant::now()
// ================================================================================================

import std;

namespace wnd = std::windowing;                 // file-local alias (30)

@std::log::level_override{ .level = std::log::level::debug };     // this file logs from debug up (31)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OpenGL: the few GL 1.1 functions this demo needs are exported by the system's GL library, so they
// are plain C imports (13). Newer functions come from group.proc_address(...) (open question 4).
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
extern(std::build::language::c) {
    void glViewport(i32 x, i32 y, i32 width, i32 height);
    void glClearColor(f32 red, f32 green, f32 blue, f32 alpha);
    void glClear(u32 mask);
    void glEnable(u32 capability);
    void glDisable(u32 capability);
    void glScissor(i32 x, i32 y, i32 width, i32 height);
    void glGenTextures(i32 count, std::raw_ptr<mut u32> textures);
    void glBindTexture(u32 target, u32 texture);
    void glTexParameteri(u32 target, u32 name, i32 value);
    void glTexImage2D(u32 target, i32 level, i32 internal_format, i32 width, i32 height, i32 border,
                      u32 format, u32 type, std::raw_ptr<u8> pixels);
}

compile_time u32 gl_color_buffer_bit  = 0x4000;
compile_time u32 gl_scissor_test      = 0x0C11;
compile_time u32 gl_texture_2d        = 0x0DE1;
compile_time u32 gl_texture_min_filter = 0x2801;
compile_time i32 gl_nearest           = 0x2600;
compile_time i32 gl_rgba8             = 0x8058;
compile_time u32 gl_rgba              = 0x1908;
compile_time u32 gl_unsigned_byte     = 0x1401;

// The context every "normal" window of this program asks for. Windows with this config join the
// same share group automatically.
compile_time wnd::opengl_config gl_33 = wnd::opengl_config{
    .version_major = 3,
    .version_minor = 3,
    .profile       = wnd::opengl_profile::core,
};

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Key bindings as annotations on methods (29), dispatched by reflection (26)
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Binds a key (with modifiers) to a method. The method is called when the key is pressed.
annotation(std::meta::target::function) struct binding {
    wnd::key       key;
    wnd::modifiers modifiers = default;

    bool operator==(binding& other) = default;

    compile_time check (annotated.parameters.len() == 0)
        else f"@binding: '{annotated.name}' is called on a key press, so it can't take parameters";
}

// Calls the method of `target` bound to `key` + `mods`. Returns false if no method is bound.
template<type T>
bool dispatch_binding(mut T& target, wnd::key key, wnd::modifiers mods) {
    // Entry check, evaluated once per instantiation (23): two methods on the same key is a compile
    // error at the @binding, not a silent "first one wins".
    compile_time check {
        for (std::meta::function a : std::meta::methods<T>()) {
            for (std::meta::function b : std::meta::methods<T>()) {
                if (a.has<binding>() && b.has<binding>() && a.name < b.name
                    && a.annotation<binding>() == b.annotation<binding>()) {
                    std::compile_error(f"'{a.name}' and '{b.name}' are bound to the same key");
                }
            }
        }
    }
    for compile_time (std::meta::function m : std::meta::methods<T>()) {
        if compile_time (m.has<binding>()) {
            compile_time binding b = m.annotation<binding>().expect("checked by has");
            if (key == b.key && mods == b.modifiers) {
                if compile_time (m.is_mut) { m.call(mut target); } else { m.call(target); }
                return true;
            }
        }
    }
    return false;
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The program's own state. Plain data: std::windowing never sees it.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@std::derive::formattable
struct app_state {
    bool running  = true;
    bool paused   = false;
    f64  player_x = 640.0;
    f64  player_y = 360.0;
    f64  zoom     = 1.0;
    u32  frames   = 0;              // frames drawn in the current second

    // Requests the bindings can't carry out themselves: they need `sys`, or they change the list of
    // windows that the main loop is walking (12: a container can't change while it's borrowed).
    bool fullscreen_requested  = false;
    bool tool_window_requested = false;
    bool sandbox_requested     = false;

    @binding{ .key = wnd::key::escape }
    void quit() mut { this.running = false; }

    @binding{ .key = wnd::key::space }
    void toggle_pause() mut { this.paused = !this.paused; }

    @binding{ .key = wnd::key::f11 }
    void toggle_fullscreen() mut { this.fullscreen_requested = true; }

    @binding{ .key = wnd::key::n, .modifiers = wnd::modifiers{ .control = true } }
    void open_tool_window() mut { this.tool_window_requested = true; }

    @binding{ .key = wnd::key::n, .modifiers = wnd::modifiers{ .control = true, .shift = true } }
    void toggle_sandbox() mut { this.sandbox_requested = true; }

    // @binding{ .key = wnd::key::space } void jump() mut { ... }
    //   → error: 'jump' and 'toggle_pause' are bound to the same key
}

// An inspector window. Destroying it (dropping it from the darray) closes the OS window.
struct tool_window {
    wnd::window win;
    u32         number;
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stand-in for the future debug UI. It only shows the two seams: input first, drawing last.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

struct debug_overlay_stub : wnd::input_layer {
    bool visible = false;

    // Sees each event before the game. Consumed events never reach handle_game_event.
    wnd::routing on_event(wnd::event e, wnd::window& win) mut override {
        return match (e) {
            wnd::event::key(wnd::key_event{ .key = wnd::key::f1, .action = wnd::key_action::pressed, .. }) => {
                this.visible = !this.visible;
                wnd::routing::consume
            },
            // While visible, the panel takes the mouse and the keyboard (a real UI asks its widgets).
            wnd::event::mouse_button(_) if this.visible => wnd::routing::consume,
            wnd::event::scrolled(_) if this.visible     => wnd::routing::consume,
            wnd::event::key(_) if this.visible          => wnd::routing::consume,
            wnd::event::text(_) if this.visible         => wnd::routing::consume,
            _                                           => wnd::routing::pass,
        };
    }

    // For state queries (win.input()), which routing doesn't filter: the game asks the UI.
    bool wants_keyboard() { return this.visible; }

    // Draws last, into the frame the game already drew. Sized by the window's content scale, so
    // it has the same physical size on a HiDPI monitor.
    void draw(mut wnd::gl_frame& frame) {
        if (!this.visible) {
            return;
        }
        f32 scale  = frame.window().content_scale().x;
        i32 width  = cast::saturate<i32>(320.0 * scale);
        i32 height = cast::saturate<i32>(200.0 * scale);
        i32 margin = cast::saturate<i32>(16.0 * scale);
        i32 top    = cast::saturate<i32>(frame.framebuffer_size().height);
        unsafe {
            glEnable(gl_scissor_test);
            glScissor(margin, top - margin - height, width, height);   // GL's y axis points up
            glClearColor(0.15, 0.17, 0.22, 1.0);
            glClear(gl_color_buffer_bit);
            glDisable(gl_scissor_test);
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Shared resources
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// RGBA8 checkerboard. Runs on a worker thread: wnd::image is plain data, so it is sendable (27).
wnd::image make_checker_image(u32 size, u32 cell) {
    mut std::darray<u8> pixels = std::darray<u8>::with_capacity(cast<usize>(size) * cast<usize>(size) * 4);
    for (u32 y : 0..size) {
        for (u32 x : 0..size) {
            u8 v = if ((x / cell + y / cell) % 2 == 0) { 40 } else { 220 };
            pixels.push(v);
            pixels.push(v);
            pixels.push(v);
            pixels.push(255);
        }
    }
    return wnd::image{ .width = size, .height = size, .pixels = move pixels };
}

// Uploads into whichever context is current. The `gl` parameter is the proof that one is: you
// can't call this without a wnd::gl_current or a wnd::gl_frame (frame.current()) in hand.
// The texture belongs to that context's share group and is usable in every window of the group.
u32 upload_texture(wnd::gl_current& gl, wnd::image& img) {
    mut u32 id = 0;
    unsafe {
        glGenTextures(1, mut &id);
        glBindTexture(gl_texture_2d, id);
        glTexParameteri(gl_texture_2d, gl_texture_min_filter, gl_nearest);
        glTexImage2D(gl_texture_2d, 0, gl_rgba8, cast::saturate<i32>(img.width), cast::saturate<i32>(img.height),
                     0, gl_rgba, gl_unsigned_byte, img.pixels.as_ptr());
    }
    return id;
}

void log_sharing(std::str label, wnd::window& win) {
    match (win.share_group_id()) {
        std::some(group) => std::log::info(f"{label}: share group {group}"),
        std::none        => std::log::info(f"{label}: no graphics context"),
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Creating windows
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

std::result<tool_window, wnd::error> open_tool_window(mut wnd::system& sys, wnd::window& owner, u32 number) {
    return std::ok(tool_window{
        .win = sys.create_window(wnd::window_config{
            .title    = std::format(f"Inspector {number}"),      // a temporary: copied by create_window
            .size     = wnd::size{ .width = 360, .height = 480 },
            .kind     = wnd::window_kind::tool(owner.id()),     // stays above its owner, no taskbar entry
            .graphics = wnd::graphics::opengl(gl_33),
            .redraw   = wnd::redraw::on_demand,                 // drawn only when something changed
            // .sharing isn't written: automatic, so it joins the owner's group (same config)
        })?,
        .number = number,
    });
}

// A window that shares nothing: another GL version and profile, and sharing::independent even if
// a compatible group existed. Textures of the other windows don't exist in it.
std::result<wnd::window, wnd::error> open_sandbox(mut wnd::system& sys) {
    return sys.create_window(wnd::window_config{
        .title    = "Sandbox (GL 2.1, independent)",
        .size     = wnd::size{ .width = 480, .height = 320 },
        .graphics = wnd::graphics::opengl(wnd::opengl_config{
            .version_major = 2,
            .version_minor = 1,
            .profile       = wnd::opengl_profile::compatibility,
        }),
        .sharing  = wnd::sharing::independent,
    });
}

void toggle_fullscreen(wnd::system& sys, mut wnd::window& win) {
    match (win.mode()) {
        wnd::window_mode::fullscreen(_) => win.leave_fullscreen(),    // back to its old size and place
        _ => {
            match (sys.primary_monitor()) {
                std::some(m) => win.enter_fullscreen(m),
                std::none    => std::log::warn("no monitor to go fullscreen on"),
            }
        },
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Events
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// One event of the game window, after the debug UI took what it wanted.
void handle_game_event(mut app_state& state, mut wnd::window& win, wnd::event e) {
    match (e) {
        wnd::event::close_requested => { state.running = false; },

        // Struct patterns pick out presses; `..` skips scancode.
        wnd::event::key(wnd::key_event{ .action = wnd::key_action::pressed, .key = k, .modifiers = m, .. }) => {
            dispatch_binding(mut state, k, m) else {          // `else` after a bool call (10)
                std::log::debug(f"no binding for {k}");
            }
        },
        wnd::event::key(_) => {},                             // released, repeated

        // Holding the right button captures the cursor (hidden, unlimited movement).
        wnd::event::mouse_button(wnd::mouse_button_event{ .button = wnd::mouse_button::right, .action = a, .. }) => {
            win.set_cursor_mode(match (a) {
                wnd::button_action::pressed  => wnd::cursor_mode::captured,
                wnd::button_action::released => wnd::cursor_mode::normal,
            });
        },

        wnd::event::scrolled(s) => {
            f64 next = state.zoom * (1.0 + s.y * 0.1);
            state.zoom = if (next < 0.25) { 0.25 } else if (next > 8.0) { 8.0 } else { next };
        },

        wnd::event::focus_changed(focused) => {
            if (!focused) {
                state.paused = true;
            }
        },

        // The paths stay in the window until asked for: only this arm allocates them.
        wnd::event::files_dropped => {
            for (std::filesystem::path& p : win.take_dropped_files()) {
                std::log::info(f"dropped {p}");
            }
        },

        // Size, position and cursor are read as state (win.framebuffer_size(), win.input()) when
        // needed. Writing `_` is a decision: new alternatives of wnd::event land here silently.
        _ => {},
    }
}

// The sandbox window: its own events and its own frame. Returns false once it should close.
bool pump_sandbox(mut wnd::window& win, mut std::darray<wnd::event>& events) {
    win.drain_events(mut events);
    for (wnd::event e : events) {
        match (e) {
            wnd::event::key(wnd::key_event{ .key = wnd::key::escape, .action = wnd::key_action::pressed, .. }) =>
                win.request_close(),
            _ => {},
        }
    }
    if (win.should_close()) {
        return false;
    }
    if (win.should_draw()) {
        mut wnd::gl_frame frame = win.begin_gl_frame();
        unsafe {
            glClearColor(0.25, 0.1, 0.1, 1.0);
            glClear(gl_color_buffer_bit);
            // glBindTexture(gl_texture_2d, shared_texture) here would be a GL error: the texture
            // belongs to another share group, and GL ids are plain integers (open question 2).
        }
        frame.present();
    }
    return true;
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Drawing (the renderer itself is out of scope; clears and binds stand in for it)
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

void draw_game(mut wnd::gl_frame& frame, app_state& state, std::option<u32> texture) {
    wnd::size fb = frame.framebuffer_size();       // pixels; differs from win.size() on HiDPI
    f32 shade = if (state.paused) { 0.05 } else { 0.12 };
    unsafe {
        glViewport(0, 0, cast::saturate<i32>(fb.width), cast::saturate<i32>(fb.height));
        glClearColor(shade, shade, shade + 0.03, 1.0);
        glClear(gl_color_buffer_bit);
        glBindTexture(gl_texture_2d, texture.value_or(0));      // shared: uploaded once, used here...
        // ... draw the world at (state.player_x, state.player_y) with state.zoom
    }
}

void draw_tool(mut wnd::gl_frame& frame, u32 number, std::option<u32> texture) {
    wnd::size fb = frame.framebuffer_size();
    f32 tint = cast::round<f32>(number % 4) * 0.05;
    unsafe {
        glViewport(0, 0, cast::saturate<i32>(fb.width), cast::saturate<i32>(fb.height));
        glClearColor(0.1 + tint, 0.12, 0.1, 1.0);
        glClear(gl_color_buffer_bit);
        glBindTexture(gl_texture_2d, texture.value_or(0));      // ...and here, in another window
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The program
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

std::result<void, wnd::error> run() {
    // ---- start: glfwInit -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    mut wnd::system sys = wnd::system::start()?;
    std::log::info(f"windowing platform: {sys.platform()}");
    for (wnd::monitor& m : sys.monitors()) {
        std::log::info(f"monitor '{m.name}': {m.mode.width}x{m.mode.height} @ {m.mode.refresh_rate} Hz, scale {m.content_scale.x:.2}");
    }

    // ---- one share group for the program's resources, made before any window ------------------
    // It owns a hidden context, so textures can be uploaded now and outlive every window.
    wnd::share_group assets = sys.create_share_group(gl_33)?;

    // ---- the game window --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    mut wnd::window game = sys.create_window(wnd::window_config{
        .title     = "Rift windowing demo",
        .size      = wnd::size{ .width = 1280, .height = 720 },
        .graphics  = wnd::graphics::opengl(gl_33),
        .sharing   = wnd::sharing::join(assets.clone()),     // explicit: count + 1, visible
    })?;
    game.set_swap_interval(1);                               // vsync, for this window only
    log_sharing("game", game);

    // ---- background work: a worker thread builds an image and sends it over --------------------
    std::channel<wnd::image> loaded = std::channel<wnd::image>::bounded(1);
    std::thread::handle<void> loader = std::thread::spawn([out = loaded.sender()]() {
        _ = out.send(make_checker_image(256, 32));
    });
    std::channel_receiver<wnd::image> arrivals = loaded.receiver();
    // std::thread::spawn([move game]() { ... })  → error: 'wnd::window' isn't std::sendable
    //                                               (its field 'thread' is a std::thread_bound)

    // ---- the rest of the program's state ----------------------------------------------------------
    mut std::darray<tool_window>       tools          = default;
    mut std::option<wnd::window>       sandbox        = std::none;
    mut std::darray<wnd::event>        events         = std::darray<wnd::event>::with_capacity(256);
    mut std::darray<wnd::system_event> system_events  = default;
    mut debug_overlay_stub             overlay        = default;
    mut app_state                      state          = default;
    mut std::option<u32>               shared_texture = std::none;
    mut u32                            next_tool      = 1;
    mut std::time::instant             last_frame     = std::time::instant::now();
    mut std::time::instant             second_started = last_frame;

    // ---- main loop ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    while (state.running) {
        // 1. Read the OS queue once, for every window. Paused: sleep until something happens.
        if (state.paused) {
            sys.wait_for(std::time::duration::milliseconds(250));
        } else {
            sys.poll();
        }

        // 2. Events that belong to no window.
        sys.drain_events(mut system_events);
        for (wnd::system_event e : system_events) {
            match (e) {
                wnd::system_event::monitor_connected(id)       => std::log::info(f"monitor {id} connected"),
                wnd::system_event::monitor_disconnected(id)    => std::log::info(f"monitor {id} disconnected"),
                wnd::system_event::gamepad_connected(slot)     => std::log::info(f"gamepad {slot} connected"),
                wnd::system_event::gamepad_disconnected(slot)  => std::log::info(f"gamepad {slot} disconnected"),
            }
        }

        // 3. Each window's own events. `events` is a separate local, so nothing borrows a window
        //    while its events are handled.
        game.drain_events(mut events);
        wnd::route(mut events, mut overlay, game);           // the debug UI goes first
        for (wnd::event e : events) {
            handle_game_event(mut state, mut game, e);
        }

        for (mut tool_window& t : tools) {
            t.win.drain_events(mut events);
            for (wnd::event e : events) {
                match (e) {
                    wnd::event::close_requested => std::log::debug(f"inspector {t.number} closes"),
                    _                           => {},
                }
            }
        }
        tools.retain([](tool_window& t) { return !t.win.should_close(); });   // dropped = OS window closed

        bool sandbox_open = match (mut sandbox) {
            std::some(w) => pump_sandbox(mut w, mut events),
            std::none    => false,
        };
        if (!sandbox_open) {
            sandbox = std::none;                              // destroys the window, if there was one
        }

        // 4. Requests the bindings left for us: they need `sys`, or they change `tools`.
        if (std::take(mut state.fullscreen_requested)) {
            toggle_fullscreen(sys, mut game);
        }
        if (std::take(mut state.tool_window_requested)) {
            match (open_tool_window(mut sys, game, next_tool)) {
                std::ok(t) => {
                    log_sharing(f"inspector {t.number}", t.win);   // the same group as the game
                    tools.push(move t);
                    next_tool += 1;
                },
                std::error(e) => std::log::error(f"can't open an inspector: {e}"),
            }
        }
        if (std::take(mut state.sandbox_requested)) {
            if (sandbox_open) {
                sandbox = std::none;
            } else {
                match (open_sandbox(mut sys)) {
                    std::ok(w) => {
                        log_sharing("sandbox", w);                // a group of its own
                        sandbox = std::some(move w);
                    },
                    std::error(e) => std::log::error(f"can't open the sandbox: {e}"),
                }
            }
        }

        // 5. Work from the loader thread: uploaded once, into the shared group, with no window's
        //    context involved. Every window of the group (game, inspectors) can use it from now on.
        match (arrivals.try_receive()) {
            std::ok(img) => {
                {
                    wnd::gl_current gl = assets.make_current();
                    shared_texture = std::some(upload_texture(gl, img));
                }                                             // gl destroyed: no context current
                game.set_icon(img);                           // the platform copies the pixels
                for (mut tool_window& t : tools) {
                    t.win.request_redraw();                   // on-demand windows: show the new texture
                }
                std::log::info(f"shared texture ready ({img.width}x{img.height})");
            },
            std::error(_) => {},                              // nothing yet, or the loader is done
        }

        // 6. Simulation: continuous input is state, not events (glfwGetKey).
        f64 dt = last_frame.elapsed().seconds();
        last_frame = std::time::instant::now();
        if (!state.paused && !overlay.wants_keyboard()) {
            wnd::input_state& input = game.input();
            f64 step = 300.0 * dt / state.zoom;
            if (input.key_down(wnd::key::w)) { state.player_y -= step; }
            if (input.key_down(wnd::key::s)) { state.player_y += step; }
            if (input.key_down(wnd::key::a)) { state.player_x -= step; }
            if (input.key_down(wnd::key::d)) { state.player_x += step; }

            match (sys.gamepad(0)) {                          // a value, read once per frame
                std::some(pad) => {
                    state.player_x += cast<f64>(pad.axis(wnd::gamepad_axis::left_x)) * step;
                    state.player_y += cast<f64>(pad.axis(wnd::gamepad_axis::left_y)) * step;
                },
                std::none => {},
            }
        }

        // 7. Draw. Each window has its own context; a frame makes it current and present() swaps.
        if (game.should_draw()) {                             // false while minimized
            mut wnd::gl_frame frame = game.begin_gl_frame();
            draw_game(mut frame, state, shared_texture);
            overlay.draw(mut frame);                          // the debug UI draws last, same frame
            frame.present();                                  // consumes the frame (`move`)
            state.frames += 1;
        }
        for (mut tool_window& t : tools) {
            if (t.win.should_draw()) {                        // on demand: rarely true
                mut wnd::gl_frame frame = t.win.begin_gl_frame();
                draw_tool(mut frame, t.number, shared_texture);
                frame.present();
            }
        }

        // 8. Once a second: fps in the title, and the inspectors redraw their numbers.
        if (second_started.elapsed() >= std::time::duration::seconds(1)) {
            game.set_title(std::format(f"Rift windowing demo - {state.frames} fps"));
            for (mut tool_window& t : tools) {
                t.win.request_redraw();
            }
            std::log::debug(f"{state}");                      // @std::derive::formattable
            state.frames   = 0;
            second_started = std::time::instant::now();
        }
    }

    std::log::info(f"bye, last position {state.player_x:.1}, {state.player_y:.1}");
    return std::ok();
}   // Destroyed in reverse order: the loader (joined), the sandbox and the tools (OS windows closed),
    // the game window, `assets` (the group's GL objects are freed with its last context), then
    // `sys`. The platform connection closes with the last of them, whatever the order.

std::exit_code main() {
    std::thread::set_current_name("main");                    // the windowing thread
    mut std::log::session logs = std::log::start(std::log::options{});
    _ = logs.add(std::log::console::make(), std::log::sink_options{ .pattern = std::log::patterns::minimal });

    return match (run()) {
        std::ok()     => std::exit_code::success,
        std::error(e) => {
            std::log::fatal(f"windowing failed: {e}");        // e.g. no_display, version_unavailable
            std::exit_code::failure
        },
    };
}

// ================================================================================================
// Open questions found while writing this demo
// ================================================================================================
//  1. Automatic sharing vs. "explicit beats implicit". sharing::automatic is the default because
//     sharing is what you want when it's possible, but which group a window lands in isn't written
//     at the call. It's visible through win.share_group_id() and a debug log line from the library.
//     Alternative: default sharing::independent, and automatic only when asked for.
//  2. Typed GL objects. GL ids are plain u32, so using a texture in a window of another share group
//     can't be caught. A wnd::gl_object<texture> that carries its group id would allow a
//     debug-mode check (and a destructor that deletes it in the right group).
//  3. Render threads. Contexts and frames are thread_bound here. Rendering a window on its own
//     thread needs a way to hand a context over (win.render_target() move → something sendable that
//     comes back), while events stay on the main thread. Vulkan avoids this; GL doesn't.
//  4. C function pointers (old draft, open question 2). group.proc_address returns a raw pointer;
//     calling it needs std::fn_ptr with C's calling convention, e.g.
//     std::fn_ptr<extern(std::build::language::c) void(u32)>. Not designed yet.
//  5. Popup positions. Multi-viewport UIs place popups in desktop coordinates; Wayland has none.
//     window_kind::popup(owner) probably needs an offset relative to its owner instead.
//  6. Text input. text(char) covers typing; IME composition (preedit text, cursor inside it) needs
//     its own events before the debug UI's text fields can support CJK input.
//  7. Event buffer growth. drain_events reuses the caller's capacity, but a burst (a drag over many
//     pixels) still grows it once. Coalescing cursor_moved per drain would bound it.
//  8. Nested type names (22 #39). wnd::window::config / wnd::share_group::id would read better
//     than wnd::window_config / wnd::share_group_id.
//  9. Routing and state. A consumed event is removed from the buffer, but win.input() still shows
//     the key as held. Should a layer be able to mask parts of the input state as well?
// 10. Vulkan surfaces. graphics::none + an unsafe win.create_vulkan_surface(instance) is the GLFW
//     shape; with std::windowing in std, the surface's lifetime (it must die before the window)
//     could be a view of the window instead of a raw handle.
